From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:41:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/30] Swallow check: an attacking-token player iteration
 covers "for each"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After the Adeline commit, Adeline, Resplendent Cathar's "for each
opponent, create … attacking that player" is a per-player iteration
(player_scope) rather than a token count, and the swallowed-clause check
reported its "for each" as dropped (a DynamicQty warning, so the card
showed as "uncertain").

CR 508.4 + CR 608.2c: a def scoped to the population that creates
tokens entering attacking, owned by the controller from before the
iteration, is the other printed shape of a "For each <population>,"
iteration: the attacked player is the iteration's referent, so no
ParentTarget consumer follows. It now counts as one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/engine/src/parser/swallow_check.rs | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/parser/swallow_check.rs b/crates/engine/src/parser/swallow_check.rs
index a891524..9a5ddab 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/parser/swallow_check.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/parser/swallow_check.rs
@@ -3662,6 +3662,24 @@ fn def_tree_co_scoped_parent_target_iteration_count(
     def: &AbilityDefinition,
     pop: &PlayerFilter,
 ) -> usize {
+    // CR 508.4 + CR 608.2c: the other printed shape of a per-player iteration:
+    // tokens made for the ability's controller once for each player of `pop`,
+    // each batch entering attacking that player ("for each opponent, create …
+    // that's tapped and attacking that player", Adeline, Resplendent Cathar).
+    // The attacked player is the iteration's referent, so no `ParentTarget`
+    // consumer follows.
+    if def.player_scope.as_ref() == Some(pop)
+        && matches!(
+            &*def.effect,
+            Effect::Token {
+                enters_attacking: true,
+                owner: TargetFilter::OriginalController,
+                ..
+            }
+        )
+    {
+        return 1 + iteration_count_below(def, pop, def.sub_ability.as_deref());
+    }
     match co_scoped_parent_target_consumer(def, pop) {
